Learned:
	1.	Fixture session runs once per execution
	2.	Fixture module runs once per file
	3.	If my tests are stored in multiple files with Test keyword, command to execute them all in one instance is "pytest -s"
	4.	if i run my tests without -s it will not show the print statements in output
	5.	fixture function runs once per function
	6.	fixture class runs once per class
	7.	fixture will be identified only when you use linkage


    8. To execute any test using commandline use following command
        - pytest Testfilename.py 

    9. To execute any test function using commandline use the following command
       - pytest Testfilename.py :: functionname

    10. To skip any test 
        @pytest.mark.skip

    11. Concept of tagging -> to run only specific set of tags, tag them with one name and after that
    you can execute them
     eg : pytest.mark.smmoke 
    
    To execute them run with command as pytest -m tagname
        - pytest -m smoke

    12. For any pytest format start the file name as Test and function name as test_ keyword

    13. Playwright has one global fixture called "playwright", which is already present in the playwright package and 
    globally recognized by ide, that will be helping you out to launch browser


  Get by label -> whenever you are identifying any label ensure it has label tag and the input should be wrapped inside
  the label tag.
  <Label> Password <input type = "Password" /> </Label>
  Or the id of input should be associated with the for of the label's input box
  if id of input and for attribute of label are same, get_label() method will work
   Eg:     <label for="username"> Username: </label>
           <input id="username" />
  if id of input and for attribute of label are not same, get_label() method will not work
    Eg :  <label for="email"> Email: </label>
           <input id="userEmail" />

